d 'SPXA': module implementing Lévy Process Algebra
d
d  spxa defines Lévy processes as Stata objects that carry their
d exact Lévy–Khintchine triplet, cumulants, and simulation
d routines. Processes are composed using +, *, and @
d (subordination); core commands define processes, simulate sample
d paths ready for xtset, and report triplets and cumulants in r().
d Because the underlying algebra is exact rather than numerical,
d composed models maintain the precision of their components while
d explicitly declaring their exactness level. The package requires
d Stata 16 or newer with Python integration enabled, alongside the
d spxa Python library. 
d
d KW: Lévy processes; jump diffusion; variance gamma; CGMY; normal inverse Gaussian; subordination; Lévy–Khintchine triplet; cumulants; simulation
d
d Requires: Stata version 16 with Python library spxa
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261122
d
d Author: Nitya Hapani,  NA
d Support: email nityahapani.tges@@gmail.com
d
f spxa.ado
f spxa.sthlp
f spxa_example.do
f spxa_py.py
f ../_/_spxa_clear.ado
f ../_/_spxa_define.ado
f ../_/_spxa_drop.ado
f ../_/_spxa_ensure.ado
f ../_/_spxa_list.ado
f ../_/_spxa_report.ado
f ../_/_spxa_simulate.ado
